  {
   "id": "FhK4bsU5AwAJ",
   "from": "Vincent van Hees",
   "author": "8d92e34685fbc6bd",
   "date": "2018-08-27T11:15:40Z",
   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] time change problem",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">If the clocks move back as a result of DST then it absolutely normal that you get double timestamps.<div>That is just how the clocks work and GGIR simply follows these conventions.</div><div><br></div><div>I do not understand why you would want to delete those data, because they correspond to real measurements and are not artifacts.</div><div><br></div><div>Vincent</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Sun, 26 Aug 2018 at 05:00, &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">guowe...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
